# <%= projectName %>

Design tokens kept in [Style Dictionary v3](https://v3.styledictionary.com/) format and built for
web (SCSS, CSS, TypeScript) and Flutter (Dart).

```
tokens/color.json        colors        (color.<type>.<item>)
tokens/spacing.json      spacing       (size.spacing.<item>, rem)
tokens/typography.json   font sizes (size.font.*), families (font.family.*),
                         weights (fontWeight.*) and line heights (lineHeight.*)
```

Edit the JSON, then rebuild:

```bash
nx build <%= projectName %>
# = npx style-dictionary build --config <%= projectRoot %>/style-dictionary.config.js
```

The outputs are committed, so apps work before the first build:

| Output | Path                                       |
| ------ | ------------------------------------------ |
| SCSS   | `<%= projectRoot %>/<%= outputs.scss %>`   |
| CSS    | `<%= projectRoot %>/<%= outputs.css %>`    |
| TS     | `<%= projectRoot %>/<%= outputs.ts %>`     |
| Dart   | `<%= projectRoot %>/<%= outputs.dart %>`   |

They are listed in the workspace `.prettierignore` so formatting never fights the generator.

## SCSS

Add the folder to the app's `stylePreprocessorOptions` in `project.json`:

```json
"stylePreprocessorOptions": { "includePaths": ["<%= projectRoot %>/generated/scss"] }
```

```scss
@use 'tokens' as t;

.button {
  background: t.$color-brand-primary;
  padding: t.$size-spacing-sm t.$size-spacing-md;
}
```

## CSS custom properties

Add the file to the app's `styles` in `project.json` (before the app's own stylesheet):

```json
"styles": ["<%= projectRoot %>/<%= outputs.css %>", "apps/<app>/src/styles.scss"]
```

```css
.card {
  color: var(--color-neutral-dark);
  gap: var(--size-spacing-md);
}
```

## TypeScript

```ts
import { ColorBrandPrimary, SizeSpacingMd } from '<%= importPath %>';
```

## Flutter (Dart)

`<%= projectRoot %>/generated/dart` is a Dart package (`<%= snakeName %>_tokens`). Depend on it by path
from the app's `pubspec.yaml`:

```yaml
dependencies:
  <%= snakeName %>_tokens:
    path: ../../<%= projectRoot %>/generated/dart
```

```dart
import 'package:<%= snakeName %>_tokens/tokens.dart';

final color = <%= dartClassName %>.colorBrandPrimary;
final padding = <%= dartClassName %>.sizeSpacingMd; // logical pixels (rem × 16)
final family = <%= dartClassName %>.fontFamilyBase; // a String
```

Font families are strings; the font files themselves still go in the app's `pubspec.yaml`. Keep
only families under `font` — Style Dictionary's Flutter transforms quote every `font` token, which
is why weights and line heights have their own `fontWeight` and `lineHeight` categories.
